  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write ASK 593" at 01:26 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread, with no run live (Wall 11442; audit 41278). Engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 9bec145c to a17c7a7b-9705-4e39-ad91-608211681c9b, 422 nodes, 17 changed, by removals only; child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT 2d5bdc94 to e9ddab5e-40ae-410f-b0a2-059799ac4d90 (Shared Library). LIB a5b27df14d596da7, MAP e6f0341b87c6190c. Then the migration mig593.sql. What is live: no engine or child node holds the word haiku. Init Seats: haiku is out of ORDER0, __ALT, ENG, FAM_PANEL and the call-family map; the rule that moved haiku to the end after the first three free seats is removed; the single judge's filter keeps "not sonnet" only. Accept Build: out of ORDER and ENG_SEAT. Resolve Seats, Build Synthesis, Build Independent Verdict and Build Diagnostic Prompt: out of the call-family map. The direct Anthropic id form in Resolve Seats and D1 to D4 and C1 to C4 Build reads claude-(opus|sonnet|fable|mythos). Format Markdown and Failure Salvage no longer name it. The Shared Library's cure-note model list loses anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5. Database: dash_debaters has no haiku row (md5 4a16cddc), so the dashboard does not offer it and dash_launch_odv1 refuses it; odv1_record_panel_substitution's seat list has no haiku (md5 1b1c2188); the model_config row haiku is kept, active false. A launch naming haiku is refused at Init Seats: 'defender engine "haiku" is not one of [claude, chatgpt, gemini, grok, mimo, opus, glm, qwen4max, spark, sol62, deepseek]'. Left as they are (W1 R1, Wall 11439): the display-order lists of dash_odv1_debates and dash_odv1_judges, which sort past judgments; the comment in odv1_record_panel_alternates; past records. Effect on the line-up (Init Seats replayed on 270 cases): haiku is seated in none; no pair that ran before is refused; 78 cases change, each one where haiku sat; four pairs (chatgpt or sol62 against gemini, both ways) keep the panel spark, qwen4max and sonnet with no reserve and no alternate. W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11443): engine a17c7a7b equals target_engine_593.json and W1's rebuild, 0 node differences, 0 nodes hold haiku; child e9ddab5e the same; dash_debaters and odv1_record_panel_substitution differ from their pre-write sources by the haiku word only; model_config haiku active false. IN PART, because no run has executed on a17c7a7b: the removal is shown by the readback and the offline replay, not by a run. The path: the operator's two messages (01:15 and 01:16 CST, W3 thread); W3's reading posted at Wall 11432 and 11433; the coordinator numbered it 593; W4's build rev 0 (Wall 11437); W1 PASS (Wall 11439); the press; the write (Wall 11442); the readback (Wall 11443). Found and not changed (scope rule; W1 R2): odv1_record_panel_substitution's seat list has never held qwen4max, and Init Seats makes qwen4max the reserve in 2 pairs after this write (16 before); a reserve used there would raise at its record. It is W4's separate question to the operator (ASK 594 on W4's card). Consequence for other work: ASK 590 must be re-cut on a17c7a7b before its write; the ASK 591 table is seeded without haiku (plan rev 4, Wall 11445). RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). The run's record names no haiku seat or model. W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule asks, for ASK 593 (agreed by W1, Wall 11785); IN PART until the second (W1, Wall 11890). In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
